#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fleet-soak: per-process memory soak sampler and verdict reporter.

Stdlib only (ctypes is used for libproc on macOS).

    fleet-soak sample --label L --exe P (--out F | --soak DIR | --start-soak DIR)
                      [--once] [--interval 60] [--proc NAME] [--probe-json FILE|-]
    fleet-soak report --in F [--seat S] [--proc P] [--window H] [--accelerated]
                      [--scenario X] [--slope-max MB/h] [--cap MB]
                      [--ports-slope-max n/h] [--max-step pct]
                      [--max-restarts N] [--min-hours 72]
                      [--min-completeness 0.95] [--validate] [--json]
                      [--cpu-max 80] [--cpu-ticks 3] [--tap-timeouts-max 10]
                      [--flips-max 6] [--unresponsive-max 20]

JSONL layout: the first line is a header
  {"header": true, "metric": "phys_footprint"|"private_bytes",
   "scenario_source": "observed", "sampler_sha": ..., "seat": ..., "proc": ...,
   "interval": 60, "restart_source": ...}
followed by one sample object per line. `restart_source` says whether
restart_count comes from launchd (`runs =`) or is null, in which case restarts
are detected only from (exe, pid, start_time) tuple changes.

On macOS a verdict is INVALID when any post-warm-up sample's metric_source is
not proc_pid_rusage (the top(1) RSS fallback measures something else).

Each sample also carries `cpu_s` (user+system CPU seconds of the process),
`cpu_pct` (derived from the previous sample of the same pid), and per-tick
log-tail deltas: `tap_timeouts` (Mouser "CGEventTap disabled by system"),
`epoch_flips` (core "promoting to server"), `unresponsive` (core
ClientProxyUnknown); `log_offset` is the byte offset the next tick counts
from. The sampler raises a desktop notification (macOS osascript / Windows
msg *) when the process is absent for 2 consecutive ticks or above
CPU_ALERT_PCT for CPU_ALERT_TICKS consecutive ticks. The report fails on the
same CPU rule and on per-hour rates above --tap-timeouts-max / --flips-max /
--unresponsive-max.

Report exit codes: 0 pass, 1 fail (criteria), 2 verdict invalid.
"""

